<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!--
    Livestock products at a fixed difficulty.

    The economic difficulty multiplies every fill type's selling price: EASY x3, NORMAL x1.8, HARD x1.
    The mod's animals never read it (the dealer and the live price curves are the same on every
    difficulty), but what they give does: on HARD meat, milk and eggs sell at a third of EASY, and so
    does a finished animal whose live price is held up by its meat.

    difficulty  The difficulty the listed fill types are sold at, whatever the game is set to: EASY,
                NORMAL or HARD. GAME uses the game's (turns this off). With EASY a game on HARD sells
                them exactly as on EASY - selling points, great demand, the farm shop - and live
                animals are priced as on EASY too, since their meat floor and market factor read
                those prices. Crops, feed, bedding, fees and every other cost keep the game's
                difficulty. Contract slaughter fees are not difficulty-scaled on any difficulty.

    The list holds the products animals give and the goods made only from them, so that processing
    still pays (a dairy's cheese stays worth more than its milk). Goods also made from crops (fabric
    from cotton as well as wool, cakes) are left out; a fill type the map lacks is ignored.

    To change it without editing the mod, copy this file to
    modSettings/FS25_RealisticLivestockRM/livestockPrices.xml; that copy then replaces this file
    entirely. In multiplayer the server's file applies.
-->
<livestockPrices difficulty="EASY">
    <!-- meat -->
    <fillTypes names="BEEFMEAT PORKMEAT SHEEPGOATMEAT POULTRYMEAT GOOSEMEAT RABBITMEAT HORSEMEAT"/>
    <!-- milk and dairy -->
    <fillTypes names="MILK GOATMILK BUFFALOMILK MILK_BOTTLED MILK_BOTTLED_SOLO GOATMILK_BOTTLED BUFFALOMILK_BOTTLED CREAM LOWFATMILK BUTTER CHEESE GOATCHEESE BUFFALOMOZZARELLA"/>
    <!-- eggs, wool, feathers, breeding -->
    <fillTypes names="EGG EGG_HB QUAILEGG CHICKS SHEEPWOOL_SHEARED SHEEPWOOL_CLEANEDWET SHEEPWOOL_CLEANEDDRY SHEEPWOOL_CLEANED GOOSEFEATHERS BULLSPERM"/>
</livestockPrices>
